// Title: Remove Scheduled Cron Task/Job
// Sigma ID: c2e234de-03a3-41e1-b39a-1e56dc17ba67
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects usage of the 'crontab' utility to remove the current crontab. This is a common
//   occurrence where cryptocurrency miners compete against each other by removing traces of other
//   miners to hijack the maximum amount of resources possible
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/22/i/how-malicious-actors-abuse-native-linux-tools-in-their-attacks.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_crontab_removal.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "crontab" and ProcessCommandLine contains " -r"
